# CRAH Unit Operation Procedure

## Equipment Information
- **Unit ID**: [UNIT_ID]
- **Location**: Building [BUILDING], Floor [FLOOR], Row [ROW]
- **Model**: [MODEL_NUMBER]
- **Serial Number**: [SERIAL_NUMBER]
- **Manufacturer**: [MANUFACTURER]
- **Installation Date**: [INSTALLATION_DATE]

## Electrical Specifications
- **Power Supply**: [POWER_SUPPLY] VAC, [AMPERAGE] A
- **Circuit Number**: [CIRCUIT_NUMBER]
- **Breaker Rating**: [BREAKER_RATING] A
- **UPS Connection**: [UPS_CONNECTION]

## Mechanical Specifications
- **Cooling Capacity**: [COOLING_CAPACITY] tons
- **Airflow**: [AIRFLOW] CFM
- **Water Flow**: [WATER_FLOW] GPM
- **Operating Pressure**: [OPERATING_PRESSURE] PSI

## Pre-Operation Checklist
- [ ] Verify power supply is available
- [ ] Check water supply valves are open
- [ ] Ensure drain lines are clear
- [ ] Verify control panel is accessible
- [ ] Check for any visible damage
- [ ] Ensure area is clear of obstructions

## Startup Procedure
1. **Power On**
   - Close main electrical disconnect
   - Verify control panel displays normal
   - Check for any fault indicators

2. **Water System**
   - Open supply water valve
   - Open return water valve
   - Check for leaks
   - Verify water pressure is [WATER_PRESSURE] PSI

3. **Control System**
   - Set temperature to [SETPOINT_TEMPERATURE]°F
   - Set fan speed to [FAN_SPEED]%
   - Enable automatic mode
   - Verify all sensors are reading

4. **Final Verification**
   - Check air temperature differential
   - Verify water temperature differential
   - Ensure no unusual noises
   - Confirm all alarms are clear

## Normal Operation
- **Temperature Range**: [MIN_TEMP]°F to [MAX_TEMP]°F
- **Pressure Range**: [MIN_PRESSURE] to [MAX_PRESSURE] PSI
- **Fan Speed Range**: [MIN_FAN]% to [MAX_FAN]%
- **Operating Hours**: [OPERATING_HOURS]

## Shutdown Procedure
1. **Gradual Shutdown**
   - Reduce fan speed to minimum
   - Allow unit to reach ambient temperature
   - Close water supply valve
   - Close water return valve

2. **Power Off**
   - Switch to manual mode
   - Turn off fan
   - Open main electrical disconnect
   - Verify all systems are off

## Maintenance Schedule
- **Daily**: Visual inspection, temperature checks
- **Weekly**: Filter inspection, water level check
- **Monthly**: Belt inspection, electrical connections
- **Quarterly**: Water treatment, sensor calibration
- **Annually**: Complete system inspection, parts replacement

## Safety Requirements
- **PPE Required**: Safety glasses, work gloves, hard hat
- **Lockout/Tagout**: Required for electrical work
- **Confined Space**: Not applicable
- **Hot Work**: Not applicable

## Emergency Procedures
- **Fire**: Activate fire suppression, evacuate area
- **Electrical Fault**: Open main disconnect, contact electrician
- **Water Leak**: Close water valves, contact maintenance
- **Equipment Failure**: Switch to backup unit, contact technician

